# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# packwiz hashes files as they sit on disk and records those hashes in index.toml.
# Without this, a Windows checkout (CRLF) and a macOS checkout (LF) hash the SAME
# committed file differently, so `packwiz refresh` on either machine rewrites ~24
# index.toml hashes and the two platforms ping-pong the diff forever.
# Discovered 2026-08-08: the v1.4.0 index.toml held CRLF hashes, unusable on macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.exe binary
*.mrpack binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
